  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "Which method is more suitable for representing all integers?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "Roster notation",
    "B": "Only drawing a diagram",
    "C": "Only writing the empty set",
    "D": "Set-builder notation"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "There are infinitely many integers, so a finite list cannot write out every integer individually. Set-builder notation is suitable:\n\\[\n\\{x\\mid x\\text{ is an integer}\\}.\n\\]\nIf “more suitable” means giving a direct description by a property, the intended choice is D.\n\nRoster notation with ellipses also represents all integers:\n\\[\n\\{\\ldots,-2,-1,0,1,2,\\ldots\\}.\n\\]\nThus D is a suitability preference, while A is also a valid representation. Without a stated preference criterion, the question does not uniquely determine a choice.",
